<header><p class="enc-kicker">People / group</p><h1 class="enc-title">Voortrekkers</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">1830s–1840s</span></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The Voortrekkers were Dutch-speaking settlers, mainly from the eastern <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/cape-colony">Cape Colony</a>, who left British rule from 1835 onwards in the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/great-trek">Great Trek</a> and moved into the interior of southern <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/africa">Africa</a>. They fought the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/ndebele-kingdom">Ndebele</a> and the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/zulu-kingdom">Zulu</a>, notably at Blood River in 1838, and founded the Natalia Republic and the states that became the South African Republic and the Orange Free State.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/voortrekkers.jpg" alt="Voortrekkers" width="320" height="274" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Discott · CC BY-SA 4.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Great_Trek_map_full.png" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
